cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  This software is a port. If it contributes to work you publish, please cite
  the R reference implementation it is ported from (listed under references
  below) and the paper behind the estimator you used, in addition to or instead
  of this port.
title: "copulaendog: instrument-free Gaussian copula endogeneity corrections for Stata and Python"
abstract: >-
  Stata and Python ports of five cross-sectional Gaussian copula corrections
  for endogenous regressors in linear models: Park and Gupta (2012), the
  two-stage copula generated regressor approach of Yang, Qian and Xie (2025),
  the between-regressor correlation variant of Haschka (2025), the
  nonlinear-transformation approach of Breitung, Mayer and Wied (2024), and the
  adjusted estimator of Liengaard et al. (2025). Ported from the R reference
  implementation of Rouven E. Haschka and from the endogCopula package of
  Ashwin Malshe.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Mallapragada
    given-names: Girish
    website: "https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=CixA1fgAAAAJ&hl=en"
version: 0.1.0
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/girishm77/copulaendog_stata_python"
keywords:
  - endogeneity
  - Gaussian copula
  - control function
  - instrument-free identification
  - econometrics
  - Stata
  - Python

references:
  - type: software
    title: "Copula-based endogeneity corrections in R"
    authors:
      - family-names: Haschka
        given-names: Rouven E.
        orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2916-9745"
    year: 2026
    repository-code: "https://github.com/HashtagHaschka/Copula-based-endogeneity-corrections"
    notes: >-
      The reference implementation this port is derived from. Every estimator,
      every CDF estimator, the bootstrap, the diagnostics and the validity
      report come from it.

  - type: software
    title: "endogCopula: Endogeneity Corrections via Gaussian Copulas"
    authors:
      - family-names: Malshe
        given-names: Ashwin
    repository-code: "https://github.com/ashgreat/endogCopula"
    notes: >-
      The packaged R version of the same estimators, which shaped how this port
      is organised and what its documented interface looks like.

